  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I believe adding the ability to include descriptions for created world instances would greatly enhance the social aspect of VRChat and improve the user experience.\n\nCurrently, users can only rely on the world's name to understand what is happening in an instance. This can be problematic for several reasons:\n\nLack of Context: World names often don't provide enough information about the specific event or activity happening in the instance. This can lead to users joining an instance expecting one thing and finding something completely different.\n\nDifficulty Finding Relevant Instances: With no way to describe an instance, it's difficult for users to find instances related to their interests. For example, it's impossible to filter for instances celebrating a specific birthday or hosting a movie screening.\n\nMissed Opportunities for Communication: A description allows users to quickly understand the purpose of an instance and whether it's something they want to join. It could also be used to share important information, such as the event date, time, and any relevant rules or guidelines.\n\nProposed Solution:\n\nI propose adding a dedicated field for instance descriptions, similar to the \"World Description\" field. This description could be:\n\nEditable by the instance creator: This allows them to provide specific information about the event or activity.\n\nVisible in the world list: The description could be displayed next to the world name, similar to how game descriptions are shown on Steam.\n\nOptional: Users could choose to add a description or leave it blank.",
